I know that in theory, with sufficient potions of gain ability and well-
enchanted rings & armor, that it's possible to get all ability scores except
Constitution up to 25.  (It is, isn't it?  +7 rings of adornment & gain
strength, +7 helm of brilliance, +7 gauntlets of dexterity.)  How about
adding an object in the next patch or version that can raise Con. levels?
Maybe a chest plate or something, something which can be worn in conjunction
with the other stuff above.

On a more pragmatic note, and in the spirit of the new pickup setup in
3.1.2, it would be nice to have a toggle for the messages usually displayed
at the top of the screen.  When surrounded by lots of beasties, or by a
few with lots of attacks, rounds of combat are often reduced to frequent
pressing of the space bar to page through zillions of --More--'s.  This
can be especially annoying when the rest_on_space option is on and you
inadvertently skip your turn at attack.  Instead, why not have an option
to have all messages for ONE round listed down the side of the screen (left-
justified) with a single --More-- at the bottom.  I can see two possible
problems with this, although they are both minor.  One might be when one
is playing on a slow system (e.g. on a 286 or over a modem) where redrawing
the screen actually takes a bit of time; there would always be the old
(current) method of message paging to fall back on.  The other might be
for people who actually like to watch the combat while it's going on, and
the combat happens to be in the upper left part of the screen.  I don't
see this happening too often, and is again remedied by simply reverting
back to the standard form of paging.  Like the idea expressed a while back
about the character buffer to prevent running into floating eyes and the
like, this idea could be invaluable in saving the gamer a lot of both time
& frustration, as well as making the game more aesthetically pleasing.

On a final side note, there's a (very) minor bug in 3.1.1.  In discover
mode when it asks if you want to keep the save file when entering a saved
game, the paging is messed up and the message tends to spill 1 or 2 lines
into the dungeon area.  A little text formatting in the code would clear
this up quickly.
